' S-570 (2026-10-16): a NULL class reference is a clean error even when other objects already exist.
' The MIR interpreter used to resolve NULL (the integer 0 the lowering stores) to heap slot 0, i.e. to the
' FIRST object the program ever created: `k.v` read that object's field. The older neg_null_* tests allocate
' no object first, so they never saw it.
CLASS Box
    PUBLIC
    DIM v AS I32
END CLASS
DIM a AS Box = NEW Box()
a.v = 9
DIM k AS Box
PRINT "before"
PRINT k.v
PRINT "unreachable"
